# ReadMy Profile Adapter Rules for Cursor & Windsurf

When the user asks to generate, audit, polish, or upgrade a GitHub Profile README:

## 1. Prime Directive: Durability & Zero Third-Party Fragility
- Never insert dynamic third-party widgets (Shields badges, Vercel apps, Heroku dynos, dynamic visitor counters, skill-icons CDNs).
- Ensure all visual banners are standalone, local SVG files stored in an `assets/` subfolder.
- Always support GitHub Dark & Light modes using `<picture>` and `(prefers-color-scheme: dark/light)`.
- Enforce WCAG 2.2 AA contrast (>= 4.5:1) between text and background.

## 2. Anti-Hallucination Law
- Do not invent any repository, metric, degree, award, or job title.
- If data is missing:
  - Role: use placeholder `{{role}}`.
  - Bio: omit prose section gracefully.
  - Repositories: cap at top 4 public repositories by stars, excluding forks.
- Never output private details (email, location, company, social handles) unless explicit user consent is confirmed.

## 3. Execution Commands
When ReadMy CLI is available in the workspace:
```bash
# Durability audit
node cli/readmy.js audit <username>

# Interactive full setup
node cli/readmy.js init

# Deterministic profile adaptation
node cli/readmy.js adapt --github <username> --template engineer --out ./profile
```
